  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A parabolic arch has a height of \\(16\\) inches and a span of \\(40\\) inches. The height, in inches, of the arch at a point \\(5\\) inches from the center \\(M,\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(15\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(15\\dfrac13\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(15\\dfrac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(15\\dfrac34\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "15"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p26.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Place \\(M\\) at the origin with the span on the \\(x\\)-axis. The arch has equation \\(y=16-ax^2.\\) Since \\((20,0)\\) lies on it, \\(0=16-400a,\\) so \\(a=\\frac{1}{25}.\\) At \\(x=5,\\) \\[ y=16-\\frac{25}{25}=15. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Place the center at the origin and write the parabola as \\(y=16-ax^2\\)",
        "Use the endpoint \\((20,0)\\) to find \\(a\\), then substitute \\(x=5\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
